# THE FUSIONS THAT OWE NO EXACT SUM. One row per suspended fusion per quantity, and NEVER more
# than one however many grounds a composer filed.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ A SUSPENSION IS A SET AND ITS REASONS ARE A BAG, and keeping them in one relation put a
#    bag where every caller wanted a set. `composition/suspension_grounds.sqlc` is the bag: one
#    row per ground, carrying `suspended_because` for anybody who needs to say WHY. This is the
#    projection onto the key that matters, and it is what an anti-join or a count should read.
#
# ⛔ THE DISTINCT IS LOAD-BEARING RATHER THAN DEFENSIVE. `every-unsized-conversion/shift-capacity`
#    files an unsearched elimination AND an unsized conversion, so it appears twice upstream and
#    is suspended once. Dropping the projection is how a count of fourteen fusions became
#    seventeen.
-- composition/suspension_grounds.sqlc projected onto the fusion it suspends.
SELECT DISTINCT g.composition, g.composed_layer, g.quantity
FROM (
    :compose(composition/suspension_grounds.sqlc)
) g
